# Hermes discovery walkthrough

The original 90-second captioned, silent walkthrough of the cross-profile session recall finding on Hermes 0.21.5, release v2026.9.24, commit f97608f178d1ffeca59860195ab7da295f7c8e5f.

The website footage is actual Chromium output captured with yyoreel 0.3.3. The probe and results screens display plain-text excerpts from the local audit artifacts. They are saved evidence, not a live Slack or model session. All test state is synthetic.

| Time | Evidence |
|---|---|
| 00:00 | Published release and audited commit |
| 00:08 | Official multiplexing documentation: Non-goals |
| 00:20 | Pinned `agent/inline_tool_executors.py`, lines 121–137 |
| 00:32 | Pinned `tools/session_search_tool.py`, lines 434–444 |
| 00:44 | Local probe binds Bob and explicitly requests Alice |
| 00:58 | Control: bare session ID does not search Alice's profile |
| 01:08 | Saved output: seven behavior tests passed |
| 01:18 | Scope of the result and next design check |

Sources and rerun command: [Discovery walkthrough](/Users/tanishqpalandurkar/Projects/yyot/verification/DISCOVERY_WALKTHROUGH.md).

## Reproduce the recording

Start the evidence server:

```sh
python3 /Users/tanishqpalandurkar/Movies/hermes-isolation-2026-10-03/serve-evidence.py
```

Then run the foreground capture and edit:

```sh
node /Users/tanishqpalandurkar/Movies/hermes-isolation-2026-10-03/record-sdk.mjs yyoreel.config.json
python3 /Users/tanishqpalandurkar/Movies/hermes-isolation-2026-10-03/compose-walkthrough.py
```

The SDK script uses yyoreel's managed Chrome, navigation/waits, cursor animation, Recorder, InteractionTimeline, and compositor. It uses ordinary device metrics without an explicit document-origin capture viewport, and Recorder's screenshot capture mode. These settings resolved blank deep-link captures and truncated clips observed with the installed CLI's default path. The separate underlying causes were not isolated. No yyoreel package or project source was changed.

The final edit trims or holds each recorded evidence screen to its listed duration and adds captions with ffmpeg. Raw recordings, timelines, source screenshots, configurations, and scripts are preserved here.

## Narrated revision

[Play the narrated version](/Users/tanishqpalandurkar/Movies/hermes-isolation-2026-10-03/hermes-discovery-walkthrough-narrated.mp4).

ElevenLabs multilingual v2, Clear American Male Narrator. Natural voice timing is preserved; the eight recorded evidence screens were retimed to paragraph boundaries determined from offline word timestamps and silence gaps. Final duration remains 90 seconds, including the conclusion hold. Both audio and video decode completely; audio peak is -1.41 dBFS.

Script, generation metadata, independent transcript, paragraph alignment, renderer and verification report are in `narration/`. Run `python3 narration/render-narrated.py` to recreate this edit from its saved inputs. The original silent cut remains available.
